; Test: What happens with DUPLICATE values?
; In MeTTa/HE, you can have multiple copies of the same fact
; In MORK/MM2, PathMap is a SET - duplicates are automatically deduplicated

; Try to add duplicate values
(num 5)
(num 5)  ; Duplicate - will this be stored?
(num 3)
(num 5)  ; Another duplicate
(num 7)

(exec 0
  (, (num $n))
  (O (max (max-num $m) $m $n)))

; Question: How many (num 5) entries exist?
; In PathMap (a set-based structure), duplicates are automatically removed
; So we should only see ONE (num 5) in the output
;
; Expected: (max-num 7)
; And only one copy of each value in the result
